          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Nakayama’s lemma
            is a family of simple but fundamental results of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            which are frequently used to lift information from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            over a point (as for example a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaf
            over a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            at that point.
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            We first state and prove a pair of fundamental geometric facts (Prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralNakayamaLemma"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FirstSpecialVersion"}
            and Cor.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SecondSpecialVersion"}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV"} Stacks 00DV
          %p As motivation, recall the following general fact:
          %p
          #GeneralNakayamaMotivation.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (motivation)
              Given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n ,
              and
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                \-modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi n
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left( M _ i \right) _ { i \in n } ,
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in n ,
                  one has
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi supp
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi 𝒱
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi Ann
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msub
                              %mi M
                              %mi i
                            %mo )
                          %mo )
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp \left( M _ i \right) \subseteq \mathcal{V} \left( Ann \left( M _ i \right) \right) .
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi supp
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %munder
                            %mo ⨂
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi n
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo ⊆
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi n
                        %mi supp
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp \left( \underset{ i \in n }{ \bigotimes } M _ i \right) \subseteq \bigcap _ { i \in n } supp \left( M _ i \right) .
            %p
              (Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              denotes the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DZ"} zero locus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi supp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp
              denotes the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00L1"} support
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ann
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ann
              denotes the
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07T7"} annihilator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+number"} Von Neumann convention
              so that, e.g., the quantification “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
